### Contrat API caméra, vidéo, modèles et événements (camera-video.md
### D73–D86). Endpoints ADDITIFS : ne jamais bumper pnex_api_contract::CONTRACT.
###
### WebSockets (hors fichier .http) :
### - device : GET /ws/camera + Authorization: Bearer <token> (D154) — poignée de main
###   Noise NNpsk0 en binaire (D156), puis frames binaires = lien Noise scellant
###   ("PXC1" seq u32 uptime u32 w u16 h u16 (LE) ‖ JPEG) ; PING/PONG texte
###   scellés ; close 4001/4002/4003/4011/4013/4014.
### - navigateur : POST /api/v1/ws-ticket puis GET /ws/camera/live?ticket=<ticket>&device=<pk> —
###   JPEG bruts en binaire, dernière frame d'abord ; close 4004 caméra inconnue.
### Contrôle : ServerMsg::CameraConfig sur /ws/device
###   {"t":"camera_config","cmd_id","enabled","framesize","quality","fps","vflip","hmirror"}.
###
### Erreurs : 400 champ-par-champ ({"fps": "range:1..25"}, "invalid",
### "required", "unique") ; 403 camera-write-forbidden / ml-model-write-forbidden ;
### 404 masqué cross-org ; 422 ml-model-missing-bytes | ml-model-load-failed |
### ml-model-inference-failed ; 502 events-unavailable.

### Caméras de l'org (réglages + état live)
GET http://localhost:5150/api/v1/cameras
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Org-Id: {{org_id}}

### Réglages (poussés live au device)
PATCH http://localhost:5150/api/v1/cameras/{{device}}/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Org-Id: {{org_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"framesize": "vga", "quality": 12, "fps": 5, "capture_mode": "continuous", "vflip": false, "hmirror": false}

### Segments enregistrés (enveloppe D14)
GET http://localhost:5150/api/v1/cameras/segments?device={{device}}&from=2026-09-29T00:00:00Z&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Org-Id: {{org_id}}

### Octets d'un segment (video/x-msvideo, MJPEG-AVI) — download=1 → attachment
GET http://localhost:5150/api/v1/cameras/segments/{{segment}}/content?download=1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Org-Id: {{org_id}}

### Suppression (blob puis ligne) — 204
DELETE http://localhost:5150/api/v1/cameras/segments/{{segment}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Org-Id: {{org_id}}

### Registre de modèles — l'ONNX est un média kind=model (upload .onnx)
POST http://localhost:5150/api/v1/ml/models
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Org-Id: {{org_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "yolox-nano", "asset_id": "{{asset}}", "spec": {"family": "yolox", "input_width": 416, "input_height": 416, "labels": ["person", "bicycle"], "score_threshold": 0.35, "nms_iou": 0.45}}

### Tester un modèle sur une image (octets JPEG/PNG) → DetectionResult
POST http://localhost:5150/api/v1/ml/models/{{model}}/test
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Org-Id: {{org_id}}
Content-Type: application/octet-stream

< ./dog.jpg

### Événements (logs O2 ev_*) — enveloppe D14 + "available"
GET http://localhost:5150/api/v1/events?stream=events&level=warn&q=door&from=2026-09-29T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Org-Id: {{org_id}}

### Flux d'événements de l'org
GET http://localhost:5150/api/v1/events/streams
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Org-Id: {{org_id}}

### Interne (runtime de flows, header x-pnex-flow-token) :
### POST /internal/flow/video-segment?org_id&device_id&node_id&stream&started_ms&ended_ms&frames&width&height&retention_days[&flow_id] (corps AVI)
### POST /internal/flow/event  (EventInput JSON) → 204
### GET  /internal/flow/ml-model/{id}?org_id=  → {model, sha256} ; /content → ONNX
